## Worksheet

**F1** — `state` object created in `newGame()`; `rand(S)` mulberry32 seeded via `S.rngState`; `endTurn()` calls productionPhase→needsPhase→eventsPhase→stormPhase→caravanPhase→checkEnd in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2** — `genMap()` builds 64 tiles from `rand(S)`; `canBuild()` checks `B.terr.includes(tile.terr)`; `adjMult()` feeds into production `mult` in `productionPhase()`. Score 2.

**F3** — chains: mine→forge (ore→metal), soilworks→greenhouse (soil+water→food); `capOf()`/`addRes()` clamp and log overflow into `S.stats.overflowLost`. Score 2.

**F4** — colonist records w/ `skill`, `fatigue`, `morale`, `job`, `work`; `workerMult()` reads `c.skill`/`fatigueFactor(c)`/`moraleFactor(c)` in production. Score 2.

**F5** — `needsPhase()` computes per-colonist food/water need; shortage sets `c.morale-=12`; morale feeds `moraleFactor()` in production; recovery via `c.morale+=3`/resting bonus. Score 2.

**F6** — 10 `RESEARCH` nodes; `req` array enforced in `buyResearch()`; `payCost()` deducts; effects read via `techMult()`, `capOf()` (logistics), `price()` (bargaining), `stormPhase()` (stormproof/bunkers), `needsTech`. Score 2.

**F7** — 12 `EVENTS`; weighted pick via `tw`/`roll` in `eventsPhase()`; 4 choice events (refugees, scout, badwater, festival) w/ differing `fx`; cooldown via `S.eventCd[ev.id]=S.turn+EVENT_CD` filtered in pool. Score 2.

**F8** — `price()` reads `S.res[r]/cap` scarcity and `S.market.drift[r]` (updated in `caravanPhase()`); `M.caravan.inv` capped/decremented; `tradeBuy`/`tradeSell` both wired to UI. Score 2.

**F9** — `stormPhase()` fires every 7 turns, `sev` grows with turn; damaged tiles fully skipped in `productionPhase()` (`if(t.damaged) continue`); `stormwall`/research reduce `dmgChance`; `repair()` spends parts and clears `t.damaged`. Score 2.

**F10** — `serialize()`→JSON to textarea; `deserialize()` validates required fields, throws descriptive errors shown in `#saveerr`. Score 2.

**F11** — `checkEnd()` win (pop≥12 & needsMet at turn 60) and lose (`colonists.length===0` or failed turn-60 check) both reachable; `score()` combines pop/research/stock/scrip/turn; `renderModal()` shows summary table. Score 2.

**F12** — `switchTab()` wired to nav + keyboard (`Digit1-5`); log lines carry `T${e.t}`; `title=` tooltips explain source formulas; `Space` ends turn; `@media max-width:420px` adapts layout. Score 2.

**F13** — `runTests()` asserts real invariants (PRNG determinism, save/load hash match, prereq enforcement, cap respected, etc.); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless turns via `greedyTurn()` and prints `stateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1** — `S.research.drills` etc. read by `techMult()`, multiplied into `productionPhase()` output every relevant turn. Score 4.

**G2** — shortage in `needsPhase()` → `c.morale-=12` → `moraleFactor(c)` used in `workerMult()` production multiplier. Score 4.

**G3** — `stormPhase()` sets `t.damaged`/`repairCost` → `productionPhase()` skips damaged tiles (zero output) → `repair()` spends parts, clears flag, restoring output next turn. Score 4.

**G4** — `price()` reads `S.res[r]/capOf()` scarcity and `S.market.drift[r]`, drift updated each caravan cycle in `caravanPhase()`. Score 4.

**G5** — choice `fx` mutate real state: `addColonist`, `addRes`, `S.colonists.forEach(c=>c.morale...)`, `S.market.discount` — not just log text. Score 4.

